    "fnd44_jones_cf_accruals": {
        "id": "fnd44_jones_cf_accruals",
        "description": "Accruals can be decomposed into discretionary and nondiscretionary\r\ncomponents. The non-discretionary component is a result of the normal course of business. However, the discretionary component is subject to managements autonomy and should be a concern for investors. The tricky part for investors is that discretionary accruals are not directly observable. Discretionary accruals can be estimated using a model like the Jones Model. However, it assumes that revenues are unmanaged. A bold assumption. The advantage of the Jones Model is that is simple and easy to implement.",
